_ terminate-interrupt U64 = 2
_ handshake-requested-control U64 = 8
_ termination-requested-control U64 = 16
_ poll-period U64 = 64
_ probe-look-period U64 = 0x100
_ finished-step U64 = U64.max
_ parse-region-mark-offset U32 = 16
_ parse-region-offset U32 = 24
_ task-locals-offset U32 = 32
_ no-local LocalId = U32.max
_ no-place U32 = U32.max
_ no-hops U32 = U32.max
_ unsourced SyntaxId = U32.max
_ no-probe U64 = U64.max
_ probe-data-type-count = 16
_ any-item U64 = 0x10ffff

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ PartOp is U32

` What the part of a machine merged with others does for a case where another calls it
` (`emit-machine-part`). A piece below calls it for a case it writes: enters it and settles it,
` enters it on the way to a case written in it, keeps it as entered, runs what an entered case
` runs and settles it or not, exits it where it is active, exits the cases written in it, and, at
` the root, exits every active case. The piece above calls it for a case a piece above writes, or
` the root, for what it and the pieces below it add there: runs the statements they add to the
` case's entry, subscribes the groups they add, tries the immediate transitions they add,
` answering whether one passed, unsubscribes those groups, runs the `do finally` blocks they add,
` exits the active cases they write below the case, enters the first case they write in it,
` answering whether one was, and, from `part-join` on, tries the groups they join the group of
` that place among the facts' groups with, answering whether a transition passed.

| part-enter = 0
| part-enter-step = 1
| part-mark = 2
| part-settle = 3
| part-step = 4
| part-exit = 5
| part-exit-below = 6
| part-exit-all = 7
| part-entries = 8
| part-subscribe = 9
| part-immediates = 10
| part-unsubscribe = 11
| part-finally = 12
| part-exit-added = 13
| part-initial = 14
| part-join = 15

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ relayed-ops [PartOp]

` What the piece above a part calls it for, for what it and the pieces below it add.
[PartOp.part-entries, .part-subscribe, .part-immediates, .part-unsubscribe, .part-finally, .part-exit-added, .part-initial]

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ EmittedLoop is Tuple

` A loop whose body is being emitted. `syntax` is its header, or the loop itself when it has
` none. `step` is where `continue` goes and `done` where `break` does. `item` is the value
` its item has in the body, of type `item-type`, when it has an item; a loop over a
` container keeps its item in the slot `kept` instead. `cleanups` is how many cleanups were
` open where the loop began: leaving it runs the ones opened since.

+ syntax SyntaxId
+ step IRBlockId
+ done IRBlockId
+ item Operand
+ item-type TypeId
+ cleanups Size
+ kept SlotId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ CountingPass is Tuple

` A loop `open-pass` began, which counts its passes from 0: the local that holds the count, the
` block that tests it, the block after the last pass, and `index`, the count in the pass being
` emitted.

+ counter LocalId
+ testing IRBlockId
+ done IRBlockId
+ index Operand

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Unit is Tuple

` Whose code the walker emits, and where the locals of its binding are. `instance` is the instance
` whose code it is, `reading` the instance whose facts are read and `source-module` the module
` whose syntax is: the function's own, except for the value of a global, which its module's main
` typed, and for the value a class writes for a property, which is typed by an instance of its own
` for each type that holds the property. `owner-type` is the receiver's type: the instance's own,
` or in a nested function that of the member it is written in, whose receiver it reads from the
` environment. `own-scope` is the scope of the instance's function, and the slots of its binding
` run from `slot-start`, `slot-count` of them. A local is a cell of the function's frame, and so is
` an argument of a body written in source: `cells` finds the cell of each slot, and `positions`
` which argument each is. `kept` finds the value of each slot that holds the middle of a chain of
` orderings, and `kept-types` its type. `lazy-flags` finds the cell of the flag of each slot that
` is a lazy local evaluated once, and `lazy-readers` the read that evaluates one evaluated by the
` first of its reads; `inlines` is whether some lazy local is evaluated by its one read. While a
` constructor gives the properties their first values, a lazy local read then is evaluated once for
` all such reads, with `fill-flags` its flag and `fill-cells` its cell. `self` is the receiver,
` when `has-self` says there is one: the first argument of a member, and the object a constructor
` has made; `takes-self` says it is the first argument. `self-type` is the receiver's class in the
` function of a lazy property, which has no instance. `running-rule` says the code is a rule of a
` class, and `deferred-type` is the class whose put-off properties are being given their values
` (`emit-deferred`). `environment` is the local that holds the environment of the function's own
` scope, where nested functions capture the locals it declares (`open-environment`), and `received`
` says the function was given the environment of the one it is written in. `lender` is the instance
` whose lazy local a nested function written in it is evaluating: the local's value is typed by that
` instance, so the unit reads the lender then, and what the value reads is read from the
` environments, as the nested function reads anything of the function it is written in.
` `open-held` is the place of the one slot holding the middle of a chain of orderings that the code
` being emitted may read. Code read as another's, such as a style rule applied to an element, is
` emitted under a unit of its own, and the unit before it is put back whole after.

+ instance InstanceId = no-instance
+ reading InstanceId = no-instance
+ source-module ModuleId = 0
+ owner-type TypeId = no-type
+ own-scope ScopeId = no-scope
+ slot-start U32 = 0
+ slot-count U32 = 0
+ cells CPointer'U32 = 0 as CPointer'U32
+ kept CPointer'U32 = 0 as CPointer'U32
+ kept-types CPointer'U32 = 0 as CPointer'U32
+ positions CPointer'U32 = 0 as CPointer'U32
+ lazy-flags CPointer'U32 = 0 as CPointer'U32
+ lazy-readers CPointer'U32 = 0 as CPointer'U32
+ fill-flags CPointer'U32 = 0 as CPointer'U32
+ fill-cells CPointer'U32 = 0 as CPointer'U32
+ inlines Bool = false
+ self Operand = 0
+ self-type TypeId = no-type
+ has-self Bool = false
+ takes-self Bool = false
+ running-rule Bool = false
+ deferred-type TypeId = no-type
+ environment LocalId = no-local
+ received Bool = false
+ lender InstanceId = no-instance
+ open-held U32 = no-place

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ UnitRun is Tuple

` What the function emitted keeps while it runs the code of another instance as its own (see
` `enter-unit`): its unit, whether its code runs where the collector never sees it, and what the
` `do` blocks it is in keep it from.

+ unit Unit
+ in-zone Bool
+ block-effects U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Match is Tuple

` The pattern the walker emits. `failing` is the block a test that fails goes to, and
` `exact-class` says a class test there passes the class alone, no subclass of it. `testing` says
` the pattern only tests its subject, as an `is` does, and binds nothing; `declaring` that the
` names it binds are locals of a declaration or of the header of a loop, and `tested` is the
` expression a test reads its subject from, or none. `arm-it` is the slot `it`
` names in the arm being emitted. `case-subject` is the subject of the match whose arms are
` emitted: `checks-row` says the type pass checked it as a row of a table, `checked-row` is its
` value, and `checked-made` the one among `made-rows` it is, or `U32.max`. `read-in-place` is the
` expression a name is read from at once, or none.

+ failing IRBlockId = no-block
+ exact-class Bool = false
+ testing Bool = false
+ tested SyntaxId = 0
+ declaring Bool = false
+ arm-it SlotId = no-slot
+ read-in-place SyntaxId = 0
+ case-subject SyntaxId = 0
+ checks-row Bool = false
+ checked-row Operand = 0
+ checked-made U32 = U32.max

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Making is Tuple

` The tuple or struct the walker gives the fields of their first values: `memory` is where it
` lies, `type` its type, `layout` its layout and `site` where it is made. `made` says which fields
` have theirs, from `mark` on, and `own` that the function is the constructor of what is made,
` whose arguments fill fields of their names. `callee` is the constructor generated for it, called
` where it is made, and `default-holder` the instance whose facts convert the defaults of the
` arguments a property's construction leaves out.

+ memory Operand = 0
+ type TypeId = no-type
+ layout LayoutId = no-layout
+ site SyntaxId = 0
+ mark Size = 0
+ own Bool = false
+ callee InstanceId = no-instance
+ default-holder InstanceId = no-instance

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Styling is Tuple

` The style rules the walker applies at a site. `element` is the markup element whose
` constructor call stores what the element is given, and `valued` the one whose call evaluates
` the values given to the style rules written on it. `gate` is the gate in force among the site's
` `site-gates`, or `U32.max`. `action` is the action of the application being emitted, which
` makes the action of each declaration whose value reads something tracked, `live` the
` application whose values are live, or `U32.max`, and `family-gated` says its declarations are
` gated by a family of rules.

+ element SyntaxId = 0
+ valued SyntaxId = 0
+ gate U32 = U32.max
+ action InstanceId = no-instance
+ live U32 = U32.max
+ family-gated Bool = false

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Scoping is Tuple

` Where the cleanups the walker runs begin. `block-base` is how many of `open-cleanups` were open
` where the block being emitted began. While a cleanup runs on a way out, `cleaning` says so,
` `cleaning-open` counts the cleanups open around it, which an error it raises runs on its way
` out, and `cleaning-top` those open where they began to run, above which are those opened in it;
` `unwinding-from` is the body of the one a panic made the way out through. While a rule of a
` class is emitted, `rule-leaving` is where a return in its body goes, with `rule-cleanups` the
` cleanups open as the body began.

+ block-base Size = 0
+ cleaning Bool = false
+ cleaning-open Size = 0
+ cleaning-top Size = 0
+ unwinding-from SyntaxId = 0
+ rule-leaving IRBlockId = no-block
+ rule-cleanups U32 = 0

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Streaming is Tuple

` The grammar the walker emits. `pattern-helper` is the helper the pattern is run with, of
` the type `pattern-helper-type`, or no type where it has none, and `helper-argument` says the
` function takes it as an argument. `marks-argument` says the function takes where to give back
` the rollback mark it holds, `marked-argument`. `rollback-mark` is the local that holds the
` rollback mark of the body being emitted (`open-marks`), and `rollback-row` the body's row;
` `storage-row` and `observer-row` are the rows of the storage and observer bodies the type pass
` recorded for it, or `U32.max`. `given-stream` is the stream a coded match runs on, of the type
` `given-stream-type`. `capture-floor` is the first place a name is kept in that the rule being
` run keeps, below which are those of the runs it is inside (`held-here`). `classing` says the
` alternatives being tried are a scan's, tried by the item each starts with.

+ pattern-helper Operand = 0
+ pattern-helper-type TypeId = no-type
+ helper-argument Bool = false
+ marks-argument Bool = false
+ marked-argument Operand = 0
+ rollback-mark LocalId = no-local
+ rollback-row U32 = U32.max
+ storage-row U32 = U32.max
+ observer-row U32 = U32.max
+ given-stream Operand = 0
+ given-stream-type TypeId = no-type
+ capture-floor U32 = 0
+ classing Bool = false

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Filling is Tuple

` The properties a constructor gives their first values. `type` is the type that holds them,
` `count` how many there are and `start` the place of the first; `filled` says which have theirs:
` 0 one with no value yet, 1 one whose value is being evaluated, 2 one that has it, and 3 a lazy one
` whose value is stale. `checks` holds the flag of each one a value may first read on some of its
` paths alone, and `trackers` the trackers of each whose value runs in a live action of its own
` (`clear-checks`). `storing` says the constructor is storing them, and `root` is the value being
` evaluated. Where that value is a line of a root `<This` whose closures read the object, `held-unit`
` is the instance that types it and `held-environment` the environment its closures are given
` (`hold-unit`).

+ type TypeId = no-type
+ start U32 = 0
+ count U32 = 0
+ root SyntaxId = 0
+ filled CPointer'Byte = 0 as CPointer'Byte
+ checks CPointer'U32 = 0 as CPointer'U32
+ trackers CPointer'U32 = 0 as CPointer'U32
+ storing Bool = false
+ held-unit InstanceId = no-instance
+ held-environment LocalId = no-local

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Machining is Tuple

` The machine the walker emits (`use-machine`): `fact` is what the type pass found of it and
` `slots` what the binder declared it keeps; `items` are its parts, `cases` its cases and `kept`
` the names each case keeps. `composite` is the composite it is a piece of, where it is merged with
` others, and `piece` which piece it is; `below` are the composites of the machines that refine it
` (`below-pieces`).

+ fact MachineFact?
+ slots MachineSlots?
+ items [SyntaxId]
+ cases [SyntaxId]
+ kept [[Atom]]
+ composite MachineComposite?
+ piece U32
+ below [MachineComposite]

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Typed is Tuple

` A value the walker emitted and its type.

+ operand Operand
+ type TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Assignment is Tuple

` What an assignment stored, which is its value, and what it was given before the store
` converted it. One that stores no value of its own has neither.

+ stored Typed = Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type)
+ given Typed = Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ LiveTrackers is Tuple

` The locals holding the trackers of a live action open where code is emitted: those it had
` when it last ran, and those it gathers now.

+ previous LocalId
+ next LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ StyleCondition is Tuple

` A condition made at the site where code is emitted: a `when` of a style rule, and the condition
` it was made under, or `U32.max`. A condition stands for itself and those it was made under.

+ when StyleWhen
+ parent U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ RuleName is Tuple

` A name a style rule applied where code is emitted takes its values by: its slot, and the local
` that keeps the value, converted, of its type.

+ slot SlotId
+ cell LocalId
+ type TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ TurnScope is Tuple

` A loop whose turn is being emitted and has an environment of its own: its scope, and the local
` that holds the environment, or in a function that yields the field of its own environment that
` does.

+ scope ScopeId
+ local LocalId
+ place U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ LiveMember is Tuple

` An attribute or argument of a markup element being made whose value was given in a live action
` of its own, and the local of the trackers of that action.

+ member SyntaxId
+ trackers LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ LivePlace is Tuple

` A property whose value a constructor gave in a live action of its own, and the local of the
` trackers of that action.

+ place U32
+ trackers LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ReadyLazy is Tuple

` The flag of a lazy local kept behind one, and the block where an evaluation of it emitted in the
` function has ended.

+ flag LocalId
+ block IRBlockId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ SharedReady is Tuple

` A lazy local nested functions capture, and the block where an evaluation of it emitted in the
` function has ended.

+ slot SlotId
+ block IRBlockId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ OpenCleanup is Tuple

` A cleanup open where code is emitted: its body, how many were open where the block that opened
` it began, what the cleanup of a `use` reads, and what the `do` blocks around it keep it from.

+ body SyntaxId
+ base Size
+ cell UseCell
+ effects U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ SiteGate is Tuple

` A gate of the site where code is emitted: its conditions, the local holding the number of the
` block it has open, or none, and the gate in force where it was entered.

+ top U32
+ block LocalId
+ outer U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ RuleValue is Tuple

` A value given to a style rule written on a markup element, as the element's constructor call
` evaluated it, its type and its node.

+ value Operand
+ type TypeId
+ written SyntaxId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ LentLazy is Tuple

` A lazy local declared inside the value of one a function written in the one declaring it
` evaluates, and the cells of its flag and its value there.

+ slot SlotId
+ flag LocalId
+ cell LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ StateCell is Tuple

` A state cell of `scope-cells` made where code is emitted, and the local that keeps it.

+ row U32
+ local LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ AroundValue is Tuple

` A value a style rule written on a markup element gave, for the rules written in it to read: its
` node, and the local that keeps it, converted, of its type.

+ written SyntaxId
+ local LocalId
+ type TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ TakenValues is Tuple

` A row of `scope-values` the function was given (`take-values`), and where the first of its
` values is among `around-values`.

+ row U32
+ first U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ RecordedLocal is Tuple

` A number the function records a value under, and the local that keeps the value.

+ number U32
+ local LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ StackBinding is Tuple

` A binding of a global `do with` binds that is open around what is being emitted, the local
` that keeps the value it replaced, and what its slot's flag holds: 1, or for an effect the number
` of the class of the fake bound (`Instances.fake-kind`).

+ bind U32
+ value LocalId
+ flag U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Rebinding is Tuple

` A cell a machine's name was bound to anew while the expansion of an exit or an entry that binds
` it is emitted, and the local it held before.

+ offset U32
+ local LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ FoundFirst is Tuple

` The first items found for a pattern, the key they were found under, and whether they depend on
` where the pattern is read.

+ items FirstItems
+ key U64
+ contextual Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Pin is Tuple

` A value evaluated before the code that reads it: the expression it is the value of, the
` value and its type. Every reading of the expression while the pin is held gives the value.

+ node SyntaxId
+ value Operand
+ type TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ WriteEach is Tuple

` A pipe that writes each item of what it reads, whose loop is being emitted: the pipe, the
` write recorded at it, what it reads and what it writes to, and the local that keeps the
` value written to, of type `sink-type`.

+ pipe SyntaxId
+ fact FactId
+ left SyntaxId
+ right SyntaxId
+ sink LocalId
+ sink-type TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ BoundValue is Tuple

` A value a pattern gave a name while the arm it is in is emitted: the slot of the name, the
` type of the value and the value, the case of a row the name stands for, or the place a
` grammar keeps what the name captured. `it` is bound to what a pattern is given while
` the pattern is tested, and to what the pattern passed in the body of its arm; `location` to
` where an arm of a grammar was while its expression is emitted.

+ slot SlotId
+ type TypeId
+ value Operand
+ cursor U32 = U32.max
+ capture U32 = U32.max

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ MatchStepKind is U32

| step-held = 0
| step-item = 1
| step-from-end = 2
| step-length = 3
| step-rest = 4

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ MatchHead is U32

| head-none = 0
| head-case = 1
| head-tuple = 2
| head-list = 3

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ MatchStep is Tuple

+ kind MatchStepKind
+ pattern SyntaxId
+ subject Operand
+ type TypeId
+ length Operand
+ carries Bool
+ position U32
+ back U32
+ exact Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ SharedArm is Tuple

+ arm SyntaxId
+ first U32
+ count U32
+ result Operand
+ result-type TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ StreamRun is Tuple

` What the parts of a grammar run over: the node of the pattern; the stream and its
` type; the buffer of its view, its type, and the address its items start at; the cursor the
` pattern starts at and the count of items, as indexes; the locals that keep how far the
` pattern read and the farthest cursor a part of it failed at; the layouts of an index, of an
` item and of the buffer; and the calls of the stream's `pattern-view` and `pattern-extend`.
` A stream that may give more input as it is read keeps the buffer, the address its items
` start at and the count of items of its latest view in locals of their own, which the parts
` read as `run-buffer`, `run-data` and `run-length` say.

+ site SyntaxId
+ stream Operand
+ stream-type TypeId
+ buffer Operand
+ buffer-type TypeId
+ data Operand
+ start Operand
+ length Operand
+ extent LocalId
+ error LocalId
+ index-layout LayoutId
+ item-layout LayoutId
+ buffer-layout LayoutId
+ views FactId = no-fact
+ extends FactId = no-fact
+ kept-buffer LocalId = no-local
+ kept-data LocalId = no-local
+ kept-length LocalId = no-local

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ StreamPart is Tuple

` What a part of a grammar gives where it passes: the cursor where it ended, and its
` value, of no type where it gives none (see `emit-stream-part`).

+ ending Operand
+ value Typed

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ bare-part StreamPart
    - ending Operand

` A part of a grammar that ends at a cursor and gives no value.
StreamPart(ending, Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type))

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ StreamCapture is Tuple

` Where a grammar keeps what a name it captures matched: the slot of the name, where
` the type pass recorded the call that makes its text, the locals of the cursors its text
` begins and ends at and, for an optional name, of whether it holds any; for a name that
` holds what a rule gave, the local that holds it; its type, and the run of the pattern. A
` name captured in repeats nested `listed` deep keeps a list for each, from the innermost
` out, the first at `levels` among the lists of captures. A name that `accumulates` keeps one
` list, which each place it is captured adds to, or adds to a list a caller keeps where it is
` `borrowed`.

+ slot SlotId
+ site SyntaxId
+ begin LocalId
+ end LocalId
+ present LocalId
+ value LocalId
+ type TypeId
+ run StreamRun
+ listed U32 = 0
+ levels U32 = 0
+ accumulates Bool
+ borrowed Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ LentCollector is Tuple

` A collector a caller lends the function a rule runs in, by a pointer among its arguments:
` the argument, the list the function keeps the collector's items and count in while it runs,
` and the count the collector held as the function began.

+ argument U32
+ level CaptureLevel
+ mark LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Borrow is Tuple

` A list a caller keeps that a name a rule accumulates adds to, as a call given a collector
` maps it: the rule's name, and the list among the lists of captures.

+ name String
+ level U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ CaptureLevel is Tuple

` The list a repeat keeps of what a name captured on each of its passes: the capture, the
` locals of the collector's items and of its size, the call that grows the items, the
` collector's type, the type of an item, the type of the list it makes, and the local of the
` context its backing keeps the items with, where it is not the collector's.

+ capture U32
+ items LocalId
+ size LocalId
+ grow FactId
+ collector TypeId
+ item TypeId
+ list TypeId
+ context LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ItemRange is Tuple

` The items of a stream from `first` to `last`, both included, as numbers.

+ first U64
+ last U64

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ do merged-ranges [ItemRange]
    - left [ItemRange]
    - right [ItemRange]

` The ranges of two lists, each in order and apart, in order and apart: those that overlap or
` touch are joined. Where one list is empty, the other is the result.
=? right if left.length == 0
=? left if right.length == 0
. merged [ItemRange]
. at-left Size = 0
. at-right Size = 0
while at-left < left.length || at-right < right.length
    . from-left = at-right >= right.length || (at-left < left.length && left-before)
        .. left-before = !range-after(left[at-left], right[at-right])
    . range = if from-left then left[at-left] else right[at-right]
    if from-left
        at-left += 1
    else
        at-right += 1
    if merged.length != 0 && range.first <= merged[merged.length - 1].last + 1
        if range.last > merged[merged.length - 1].last
            merged[merged.length - 1] = ItemRange(merged[merged.length - 1].first, range.last)
        continue
    merged += range
= merged

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ range-after Bool
    - range ItemRange
    - other ItemRange

` Whether a range sorts after another: it starts later, or as early and ends later.
range.first > other.first || (range.first == other.first && range.last > other.last)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ do ranges-meet Bool
    - left [ItemRange]
    - right [ItemRange]

` Whether two lists of ranges, each in order and apart, share an item.
. at-left Size = 0
. at-right Size = 0
while at-left < left.length && at-right < right.length
    if left[at-left].last < right[at-right].first
        at-left += 1
    else if right[at-right].last < left[at-left].first
        at-right += 1
    else
        = true
= false

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ do single-range [ItemRange]
    - first U64
    - last U64

` A list of one range.
. ranges [ItemRange]
ranges += ItemRange(first, last)
= ranges

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ FirstItems is Tuple

` What the reference knows of the items a part of a grammar may start with, as it
` judges which alternatives of a choice to skip: whether it knows them, whether the part may
` pass where it reads none, and the ranges they lie in, in order and apart; and how far past
` where the part is tried it counts the part as read where it is skipped, `no-probe` where it
` does not know.

+ known Bool
+ nullable Bool
+ ranges [ItemRange]
+ probe U64

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ guards Bool
    - first FirstItems

` Whether the reference skips an alternative that starts so where the item at the cursor is
` not one it may start with: where it knows them, there are some, and it must read one.
first.known && !first.nullable && first.ranges.length != 0

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ SharedFirst is Tuple

` What the pattern of a rule may start with for the instance that reads it, judged where no
` call met in judging it was cut, which the reference shares among all the patterns it emits;
` and the next one kept for another instance of the same pattern.

+ owner InstanceId
+ found FirstItems
+ next U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ CaseCursor is Tuple

` A name a pattern bound to the case of a row of a table of unions: the row, its type, the
` place of the union's table layout and the case. The name reads and writes the row's cells;
` used as a value, the case is gathered from them. Once gathered, TypeScript reads the name
` from the newest of what it gathered that dominates, though the cells change, and elsewhere
` from the cells, gathering it again as a value (`gathered-at`). A row the subject `t[i]` read is `checked`:
` TypeScript checked its storage there, and the name reads and writes the columns found then,
` with no metadata.

+ row Operand
+ type TypeId
+ place U32
+ case-index U32
+ checked Bool
+ columns Operand
+ index Operand

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ CaseGather is Tuple

` A case a name stands for, gathered from its row's cells: the name's cursor among the case
` cursors, the value made and the block it was made in.

+ cursor U32
+ value Operand
+ block IRBlockId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ LandingPad is Tuple

` A landing pad some check of the function branches to, and how many cleanups were open
` where the check is: the pad runs those, newest first, before the panic leaves the function.
` `site` is the node of the first check that made it, or none: a main reports a panic that
` has no source as raised there. A pad is `unsourced` where its first check is at no node
` and keeps none: the pad of no cleanups of a spawned task's body, whose first check is where
` the body starts, and a pad a panic raised in a cleanup is resumed at where its block ends.
` `module` is the module whose tree `site` is in, which is another's where the function writes
` that module's code, as a style rule of a theme of another module applied in a main.

+ block IRBlockId
+ cleanups Size
+ site SyntaxId
+ module ModuleId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ TableMeta is Tuple

` What says whether a table, or a view of one, can still be read: the header an arena's table
` keeps, zero for a table that does not grow, the arena that owns it, the arena's incarnation
` and generation when the value was made, and the table's shrink generation then.

+ header Operand
+ owner Operand
+ incarnation Operand
+ generation Operand
+ shrink Operand

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ TableCursor is Tuple

` A row of a table read at `t[i]` and not yet made a value, as TypeScript's cursor is: the
` columns, found and checked, the index, checked against the length, and the metadata of the
` table.

+ columns Operand
+ index Operand
+ meta TableMeta

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ MadeRow is Tuple

` A row of a table made a value, in memory of the frame that nothing writes once it is made, and
` the cursor it was made from.

+ value Operand
+ cursor TableCursor

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ TableSource is Tuple

` The rows of a table or of a span of one, as TypeScript reads them: the columns, found and
` checked, the first of the rows, how many there are, and the metadata.

+ columns Operand
+ offset Operand
+ length Operand
+ meta TableMeta

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ProvenTable is Tuple

+ loop SyntaxId
+ kind IntrinsicKind
+ source TableSource

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ProvenColumn is Tuple

+ loop SyntaxId
+ column U32
+ local LocalId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ProvenRead is Tuple

+ loop SyntaxId
+ column U32
+ block IRBlockId
+ value Operand
+ type TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ ProvenItem is Tuple

+ loop SyntaxId
+ slot SlotId
+ columns Operand

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ BuilderItems is Tuple

` Where the items of an arena's builder are kept, and how many fit there.

+ storage Operand
+ capacity Operand

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ UseCell is Tuple

` What the cleanup of a `use` reads: the flag that says its cell holds an object, the object
` and its type. The cleanup of a `do use` has no flag, since its object is there from the
` moment it opens. A `use` in a generator has no cells: its slot keeps the object. Any other
` cleanup has none of these.

+ flag LocalId
+ held LocalId
+ type TypeId
+ is-live-call = false

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ Refused is Error

` Raised where a function has no shape, once its refusal is recorded.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ Emitter

` Builds the IR of each function a worker takes into `ir`, each with a `FunctionEmitter` of its
` own, and says whether the last was refused (`refusal`) or built as a bridge (`bridged`). It keeps
` what lasts from one function to the next: `type-values`, the types whose values the functions name;
` the first sets of the patterns they share (`shared-first-heads`); and what the code of the
` functions a bridged member calls does to storage, which `probe` builds in `probe-storage`: `scans`
` holds what was found for the functions of `scanned`. `lists` are the collections each walker
` fills, emptied as each walk begins.

+ ir IRFunction
+ refusal Refusal
+ bridged Bool
+ type-values [TypeId]
_ shared-first-heads Map'U64'U32
_ shared-firsts [SharedFirst]
_ probe Emitter? = null
_ probe-storage Arena? = null
_ scanned [U32]
_ scans [CalleeScan]
_ lists = WalkerLists()
_ tables ProgramTables
_ program Program
_ instances Instances
_ facts Facts
_ types Types
_ bindings Bindings
_ storage Arena

────────────────────
+ This
    - tables ProgramTables
    - program Program
    - instances Instances
    - facts Facts
    - types Types
    - bindings Bindings
    - storage Arena

.. ir = IRFunction(storage)

────────────────────
+ begin-using

this

────────────────────
+ do end-using

release()

────────────────────
+ do release

if probe-storage
    probe-storage.release()

────────────────────
+ get is-refused Bool

refusal.construct != .refused-nothing

────────────────────
+ do emit
    - id FunctionId

` Builds a function's IR. A member that runs on a row's case, reading its cells with no check,
` is built again as a bridge to the member's instance on the case where it may move the row's
` storage before it reads the row again, as TypeScript builds its
` `table-row-receiver-bridge`. One with no such instance is refused there, and so is one
` whose code does not decide it, unless nothing would show which it is built as.
bridged = false
. built = build(id)
if is-refused || built.row-columns == U32.max
    =
. watched [U32]
watched += 0
watched += built.row-columns
. reads = receiver-reads(ir, watched)
. judged = receiver-callees(ir, tables, instances, program, reads)
. verdicts [Stability]
for callee in judged
    verdicts += judge(callee)
. verdict = receiver-stability(ir, tables, instances, program, reads, watched, judged, verdicts)
if verdict == .stable
    =
. held = instances.rows[built.unit.instance]
if held.materialized == no-instance || (verdict == .unsure && built.function.may-panic)
    . written = held.subtree
    . site = if written.count != 0 then written.start + written.count - 1 else 0
    refusal = Refusal(.refused-function, built.unit.source-module, site)
    =
bridged = true
build(id)

────────────────────
+ do emit-fused
    - id FunctionId
    - read LayoutId

bridged = false
walk(id, true, true, read)

────────────────────
_ do judge Stability
    - callee FunctionId

` What a call of a function judged by its own code may do to storage: it may move storage
` where the function's code may, or that of any function it calls in turn.
. seen [U32]
. waiting [U32]
waiting += callee
. verdict = Stability.stable
while waiting.length != 0
    . next = waiting[waiting.length - 1]
    waiting.pop()
    if seen.find(next) != null
        continue
    seen += next
    . scan = scan-of(next)
    if scan.stability == .unstable
        = .unstable
    if scan.stability == .unsure
        verdict = .unsure
    for found in scan.callees
        waiting += found
= verdict

────────────────────
_ do scan-of CalleeScan
    - callee FunctionId

` What a function's own code does to storage, from its code as `probe` builds it, once.
for position in 0 .. < scanned.length
    if scanned[position] == callee
        = scans[position]
if !probe
    . made = Arena()
    probe-storage = made
    probe = Emitter(tables, program, instances, facts, types, bindings, made)
probe-storage!.reset()
probe!.build(callee)
. none [U32]
. found = CalleeScan(.unsure, none)
if !probe!.is-refused
    found = own-stability(probe!.ir, tables, instances, program)
scanned += callee
scans += found
= found

────────────────────
_ do build FunctionEmitter
    - id FunctionId

` Builds a function's IR as `emit-function` does. A local rule's function is built first
` with no environment, the locals nested functions capture kept as its own: each call of
` it would make one that nothing else reads. Where that has no shape, as where it writes a
` nested function, which is given the environment, it is built again with one.
. shared = tables.functions[id].kind == .lazy-rule || tables.functions[id].kind == .rule-adapter
. built = walk(id, shared)
=? built if !shared || !is-refused
= walk(id, false)

────────────────────
_ do walk FunctionEmitter
    - id FunctionId
    - unshared Bool
    - fusing Bool = false
    - fused-read LayoutId = no-layout

` Builds a function's IR with a walker of its own, and notes whether it was refused.
//emit.walks ++
lists.empty()
. walker = FunctionEmitter(this, unshared, bridged, fusing, fused-read)
refusal = Refusal()
walker.emit-function(id)
    catch Refused
        refusal = walker.refusal
= walker

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ WalkerLists

` The collections a walker fills as it builds a function. A worker's `Emitter` keeps one set,
` which every walker it builds takes as its own, and empties it as each walk begins, so that a
` walk allocates none of them and each keeps the room it grew to. A walker may point one of its
` own at another list, as a state machine's are; the set keeps the one it had.

