emit-value(body, 0)

────────────────────
_ do kept-root Operand
    - body SyntaxId

` The batch the function that builds a row, or what a line gives a slot, is built under, read
` from the local the type pass found it kept in, or nothing.
. root = facts.region-root-of(unit.reading, body)
= if root then read-captured(root.slot, body, root.batch).operand else make-operand(.operand-void, 0)

────────────────────
_ do emit-filling
    - declared SyntaxId
    - body SyntaxId

` The body of the function that fills an object with the markup written in its class: the
` builders of slots the functions it writes reach are kept (`keep-builders`), the state cells and
` values of rules it is given are kept (`take-cells`, `take-values`) and those of the `when`s
` around the rules written in rules its
` own markup brings are made and bound (`bind-cells`), the function of
` the class above is run on the object, where the type pass kept its call (`run-above`), then
` the lines of the class's own markup are run as content of the object, those of its `• This`
` where that writes them, with the state machines written beside a root `<This` where they are
` written among the root's lines, and then the rules of the class that wait for them.
. type = instances.rows[unit.instance].self-type
keep-builders(declared)
take-cells(declared)
take-values(declared)
make-cells(0)
bind-cells(0, unit.self)
. above = facts.filler-of(unit.reading)
if above != no-fact
    run-above(declared, above, type, body)
content-hosts += Typed(unit.self, type)
for machine in tree.root-machines(declared, false)
    emit-statement(machine)
if body != 0
    emit-block(body, tree.nodes[declared] is .node-rule-syntax)
for machine in tree.root-machines(declared, true)
    emit-statement(machine)
content-hosts.pop()
run-markup-rules(type, declared)
emit-end(declared)

────────────────────
_ do keep-builders
    - declared SyntaxId

` Keeps, in the environment, the function that builds each slot this function was given that a
` function written in it reaches through the local that holds it.
for offset in 0 .. < unit.slot-count
    . slot = unit.slot-start + offset
    if bindings.slots[slot].kind != .slot-builder || !owns(slot) || !is-captured(slot)
        continue
    . position = instances.slot-argument(unit.instance, bindings.slots[slot].name)
    if position == U32.max
        continue
    . type = instances.argument-type(unit.instance, position)
    if type != facts.slot-type(unit.instance, offset)
        refuse(.refused-conversion, declared)
        =
    keep-captured
        - slot
        - make-operand(.operand-argument, if unit.takes-self then position + 1 else position)
        - type
        - declared

────────────────────
_ do run-above
    - declared SyntaxId
    - call FactId
    - type TypeId
    - body SyntaxId

` Runs, on the object, the function that fills it with the markup of the class above, given the
` state cells this function was given, and the builder of each slot it takes, in the order it
` takes them: the one this function was given for the slot, or else the function of the line of
` its own markup that gives the slot content, made the `MarkupSlotBuilder` the type pass
` recorded at the line. Making these runs nothing.
. callee = facts.calls[call].callee
. slots = instances.rows[callee].slots.count
. carried = instances.rows[callee].carried
if slots == 0 && carried == 0
    call-protocol(declared, call, unit.self, type, make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type, false)
    =
. above = instances.rows[callee].self-type
if !is-callable(callee) || odd-arity || carried != instances.rows[unit.instance].carried || unrelated
    refuse(.refused-statement, declared)
    =
.. odd-arity = instances.signatures[callee].args.count != carried + slots
.. unrelated = !tables.is-class(type) || !tables.is-class(above) || !tables.derives(type, above)
. mark = pending.length
pending += unit.self
for offset in 0 .. < carried
    . argument = instances.value-argument(unit.instance, offset)
    pending += make-operand(.operand-argument, if unit.takes-self then argument + 1 else argument)
for offset in 0 .. < slots
    . name = instances.slot-name(callee, offset)
    . argument = instances.slot-argument(unit.instance, name)
    if argument != U32.max
        if instances.argument-type(unit.instance, argument) != callee-argument
            refuse(.refused-conversion, declared)
        .. callee-argument = instances.argument-type(callee, carried + offset)
        pending += make-operand(.operand-argument, if unit.takes-self then argument + 1 else argument)
        continue
