= Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type)

────────────────────
_ do end-generator
    - declared SyntaxId

` What the function that ends a generator does once its own body has run. A generator that
` has not finished is given the step that runs the cleanups open where it waits, and is
` called once more: it runs them and has finished. One that has not started runs nothing
` then. The receiver is the generator, a value of a function type whose data is the
` environment that keeps the step after its link.
